# Every setting the installed service is given, and nothing else.
#
# One list, read by every installer: `ops/lyra-server.sh` (macOS launchd) and
# `ops/lyra-server-linux.sh` (systemd). It used to be a `for key in ...` loop inside the macOS
# script, which meant a second platform was a second copy — and a copy of a list like this is how
# one of them ends up missing a key. A variable absent here is not an error anywhere: it is set in
# `.env.local`, it works under `cargo run`, and it is silently gone in production with nothing
# saying why. That has already happened once, to DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL and the Google OAuth keys.
#
# `the_install_script_forwards_every_setting_the_server_reads` in crates/lyra-api/src/main.rs reads
# this file and fails, naming the variable and the source file, if the code grows a setting that is
# not listed. Add it here, or add it to that test's `excluded` list with a reason.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
#   PORT, LYRA_DB, LYRA_UI_DIR   set by each installer from its own install layout
#   LYRA_HTTP_CACHE              points the chain client at recorded test responses
#   LYRA_HTTP_FIXTURES           likewise — forwarding either would let a stray line in
#                                .env.local make production report fixture balances as your money
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. One KEY per line, no values.

# Refuses to start without this; rotating it logs everyone out.
JWT_SECRET

# Wealth — the book, and the exchange it reads (read-only keys; nothing here places an order).
ALERT_WALLETS
KUCOIN_API_KEY
KUCOIN_API_SECRET
KUCOIN_API_PASSPHRASE

# Delivery. Unset, the sweep still runs and records state without sending, which is what you
# want on a first boot.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
TELEGRAM_OWNER_USER_ID
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL

# When the box does things on its own. DIGEST_HOUR and HABITS_NUDGE_HOUR are *local* hours, so
# they depend on the host's timezone being right.
ALERT_INTERVAL
ALERT_FEE_USD
ALERT_HF
ALERT_REPORT_CCY
DIGEST_HOUR
HABITS_NUDGE_HOUR
SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL
SNAPSHOT_GROUP
LYRA_JOBS

# Knowledge notes — a git repo the module commits into.
LYRA_KNOWLEDGE_PATH

# Google Calendar. Without the first three the OAuth endpoints answer "not configured" and the
# rest of the app is unaffected. GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI must match the Console byte for byte.
GCAL_API_KEY
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI

# Where the OAuth callback sends the browser, and who may call the API cross-origin. Serving the
# UI from the binary makes the browser same-origin, so CORS_ORIGINS only matters for direct API
# access — a phone on the LAN, or a local `npm run dev` pointed at this host.
FRONTEND_URL
CORS_ORIGINS

RUST_LOG
